selectivity. Memory scales as (materializations x source rows), not with matched rows.

## Root cause

`hyphae/src/traits/collections/internal/map_runtime.rs:19` ‚Äî `MapState`:

    source_rows:        FxHashMap<SK, SV>,             // every source row
    source_output_keys: FxHashMap<SK, FxHashSet<OK>>,  // per projected source key
    output_cache:       FxHashMap<OK, OV>,             // only matches

`apply_source_diff` (same file, :39) inserts every source row unconditionally;
`MapDiff::Initial` mirrors the whole source map before the predicate is consulted.

## Measured (hyphae 2.0.1, features = ["scheduler"], release)

Source CellMap<Arc<str>, Arc<Row>>, materialized `select` holding the result:

  fixed N=25000, vary M (predicate matches 1%):
    m=1    1012 KiB/select
    m=10   1124 KiB/select
    m=50   1008 KiB/select
    m=100   989 KiB/select      -> linear in M, ~1 MB each for 250 matched rows

  fixed N=25000 M=50, vary match%:
    1%     1008 KiB/select  (250 matched)
    10%    1641 KiB/select
    50%    4205 KiB/select
    100%   6379 KiB/select  (vs 5704 KiB for the source map itself)

  fixed M=50 match%=1, vary N:
    N=5000    311 KiB/select
    N=10000   533 KiB/select
    N=25000  1008 KiB/select
    N=50000  1915 KiB/select   -> linear in SOURCE size

Decomposes to a fixed floor of ~40 bytes per source row (the mirror, paid even when
nothing matches) plus ~215 bytes per matched row.

## Proposed fix: stateless path for key-preserving filters

The mirror exists because `recompute_impacted` is generic over
`FO: Fn(&SK, &SV) -> Vec<(OK, OV)>` ‚Äî projections that fan out or rekey genuinely need
the source value to recompute.

`select` is neither. It is key-preserving and 1:0-or-1, and `MapDiff` already carries
everything needed (`cell_map.rs:29`):

    Remove { key, old_value }
    Update { key, old_value, new_value }

So for a value-only predicate:
  - Insert -> test `value`, emit if match
  - Update -> test `old_value` and `new_value`, emit insert/remove/update
  - Remove -> test `old_value`, emit remove if it had matched
  - Initial -> test each, emit matches

No source state required. Specializing this path drops both `source_rows` and
`source_output_keys` for select stages, leaving `output_cache` sized by matches.

## Secondary suspect (not measured)

`CellMapInner::key_cells` (`cell_map.rs:56`) ‚Äî DashMap<K, WeakCell<..>> whose own
doc-comment warns of "an unbounded leak on maps with high key churn", mitigated by an
amortized sweep in `maybe_prune_key_cells`. Worth confirming the sweep keeps pace under
sustained churn.

## Impact

Found while investigating a downstream deployment holding ~82k entity records across 156
types in tens of GB of RSS ‚Äî a 100-1000x amplification over data at rest. Per-stage source
mirroring across many cached query instantiations is a strong candidate for the dominant
term. Chained operators multiply it further, since each stage has its own MapState.

